# HISTORY-NOTICE-STOP: provider-carry-back with the first turn after the switch
# stopped before its request. The conversation starts on the provider that
# seals its reasoning (fx on codex, xfx on llmux), reads a file and answers,
# then `/provider` moves to the Gateway, whose catalog answers 10 s after it
# is asked: the next prompt waits at its start for that first load (a window
# nobody else gives, `orchestrator.zig:5665-5666@481104fd`), and Ctrl-C lands
# 0.7 s into the wait. Upstream ends that turn interrupted and sends nothing
# (`:5893-5919`); the prompt after it, once the catalog is in, is answered.
# xfx says once per conversation that the llmux reasoning was not carried
# (src/session/store.rs; fx drops it silently, `projectProviderReplay`,
# `types.zig:1668-1680`): the stopped turn shows nothing, so the turn after it
# says it. The turns file has no answer for the stopped turn: a request it
# sent would take the next turn's.
fx: seed provider-carry-back-fx.json
xfx: seed provider-carry-back-xfx.json
fx: homefile .fx/chatgpt-auth.json provider-carry-chatgpt-auth.json
fx: env FX_E2E_OPENAI_CODEX_MODELS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:@PORT@/codex/models FX_E2E_OPENAI_CODEX_RESPONSES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:@PORT@/codex/responses
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
nomodel
modelsdelay 10000
gateway provider-carry-back-stop-turns.json
work provider-carry-ws
wait 6
type read the notes and tell me what they say
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn1
type /provider
key Enter
wait 4
key Enter
wait 3
fx: key Down
fx: wait 1
fx: key Enter
fx: wait 3
fx: key Enter
wait 2
type what day was it again?
key Enter
wait 0.7
key C-c
wait 1
snap stopped
until gone press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 9
type and after the stop?
key Enter
wait 15
snap next
home end
gwlog
type /quit
key Enter
wait 3
